WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.700
Solo: A Star Wars Story was pitched to audiences
as a look into the early life and times of

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.819
Han Solo.

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:09.480
But Star Wars fans got a lot more of the history
from the world around Han than they might

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.019
have been expecting, and nothing was more
unexpected than the return of Darth Maul.

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:18.440
While Maul's appearance didn't have much of
an effect on Solo's story, it suggests huge

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.480
implications for the way the Star Wars saga
will unfold down the line.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.750
Let's break down what Darth Maul's appearance
in Solo means for the future of Star Wars.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.850
Criminal circle

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.020
The most direct plot consequence of Darth
Maul's return has everything to do with his

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.750
new day job: Running a criminal enterprise.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:42.079
In Solo, Maul is the shadowy leader of the
crime syndicate Crimson Dawn, with Dryden

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:45.659
Vos and Qi'ra near the top of the organization's
hierarchy.

00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:49.780
Other than Crimson Dawn, the galaxy plays
host to groups like the Mandalorian Death

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.480
Watch, the Hutt Clan, and the Pyke Syndicate,
with the Pykes facilitating the smuggling

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.229
of spice out of Kessel.

00:00:56.229 --> 00:01:01.460
The other two organizations have ties to very
familiar Star Wars characters, the Mandalorian

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.740
Boba Fett and Jabba the Hutt, both of whom
eventually end up having dealings with Han

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.820
Solo.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.770
Considering that a Boba Fett movie is in the
making and a Jabba appearance is clearly set

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.390
up by the end of Solo, the intersecting crime
syndicates appear to be an ideal way to connect

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:19.670
the different Star Wars stories back into
a larger world, with an underground criminal

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:22.310
web pulling the sprawl together.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.770
Everything is connected

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.289
For fans who only watched the movies, Darth
Maul has long been out of the picture.

00:01:28.289 --> 00:01:33.030
Obi-Wan Kenobi cut him in half, and then both
pieces of him fell into the unknown depths

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.140
of Naboo.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.780
But as his appearance in Solo indicates, the
movies aren't all that matters anymore.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.930
While tons of Star Wars lore outside of the
main series of films was jettisoned after

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:48.340
Disney purchased Lucasfilm, Darth Maul remained
in the animated, canonical Clone Wars.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:52.590
He survived his thrashing at the hands of
Obi-Wan Kenobi thanks to the force of the

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:53.590
Dark Side.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:57.920
Maul ended up being transported to a trash
planet, where he passed the time by constructing

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.590
himself a set of robot spider legs.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.659
Maul went on to become a pivotal character
in the Star Wars: The Clone Wars animated

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:08.750
TV series, as well as its follow-up, Star
Wars: Rebels.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.879
While those shows have been canonical as far
as Disney is concerned, few characters who

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:17.900
have spent so much time on the small screen
have returned to the big one, until now.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.400
The fact that Maul's story is now being folded
back into the movies has huge implications

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.550
for the rest of the Star Wars canon.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.340
Suddenly, all the characters from Disney's
Expanded Universe feel like fair game to get

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.980
called up to the movies' major leagues, and
that's never really been a possibility before.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.060
Versus Obi-Wan

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.440
Maul's appearance in Solo won't necessarily
be explored in a Solo sequel.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:44.390
After all, Han Solo and Darth Maul aren't
known for their dealings together.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.920
Maul's real nemesis, of course, is the man
who chopped him up in the first place, Obi-Wan

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:49.920
Kenobi.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.810
Maul's quest for vengeance against the self-exiled
Jedi dominated his story in Star Wars: Rebels,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:59.670
which canonically takes place several years
after the events of Solo: A Star Wars Story.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:05.390
That quest for revenge comes to fruition in
the Star Wars: Rebels episode "Twin Suns,"

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:08.890
with Maul finally tracking down Obi-Wan on
Tatooine.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:14.019
Their duel doesn't end well for Maul, with
Obi-Wan dispatching him almost effortlessly.

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:17.900
But even though we know where Maul's story
ends up, there's still a lot of story left

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.440
to tell, with years' worth of gaps to fill.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:24.890
With a potential Obi-Wan movie on the horizon,
could Maul's story continue in that film?

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.870
Rumors indicate that the Obi-Wan movie is
currently in pre-production, scheduled to

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:31.540
be filmed after Episode 9 wraps.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.540
It's all subject to change, but it feels compelling.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:39.750
Crime lord or not, Maul doesn't really belong
in a Solo sequel, not as much as Jabba and

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.550
his people, or the bounty hunter Boba Fett.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:47.150
But an Obi-Wan movie is a perfect fit, and
may be where we can expect Maul's story to

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.250
properly pick up next.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.099
Magical new worlds

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:55.890
At the conclusion of Solo, Maul summons Qi'ra
to come and meet with him on his home planet

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:00.599
of Dathomir, a world previously unseen on
the big screen.

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:06.049
Dathomir has played host to a number of malevolent
Force users, not Jedi, not Sith, but something

00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:07.049
in between.

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:11.860
Along with his brother Savage Opress, Maul
was raised on the planet by a society called

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:17.100
the Nightsisters, Force-sensitive witches
who used Dathomir's strange energies to wield

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.560
potent magic.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.660
The existence of wizardry on the fringes of
the Force is an aspect of Star Wars that's

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:28.110
remained relatively unexplored in the movies,
where any mystic character has typically been

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:29.780
either a Jedi or a Sith.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:33.150
But in the Expanded Universe, the Force is
more like a spectrum.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:37.940
For one thing, there's the existence of Gray
Jedi who draw from both the light and dark

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.449
sides of the Force.

00:04:39.449 --> 00:04:44.039
Additionally, the Force-sensitive Chirrut
in Rogue One also broadened our understanding

00:04:44.039 --> 00:04:46.229
of how the Force manifests.

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:49.800
Maul's story could further that developing
understanding in the movies.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.470
His home world would be a perfect venue for
expanding Star Wars' presentation of the mystical,

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:59.199
adding some mystery back to the Force by demonstrating
that it's not always as simple as a light

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:00.979
side and a dark.

00:05:00.979 --> 00:05:01.979
Thanks for watching!

00:05:01.979 --> 00:05:04.430
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.111
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

